" :question/math-academy-id "q-166770" :question/problem "Monica bought $10\\,\\text{m}$ of cotton fabric and paid $$39.50.$ What is the price per meter of cotton fabric?\n\nExpressed as a **decimal number**, a meter of cotton fabric costs $ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The meter of cotton fabric costs $$(39.50÷10).$\n\nTo perform this division, all we need to do is move the decimal point one place to the left:\n\n$$\n39.50\\to 3.950=3.95\n$$\n\nTherefore, $39.50÷10=3.95.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70597078-f4fd-5d33-b6e1-7b9efe3946fd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70597078-f4fd-5d33-b6e1-7b9efe3946fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "70597078-f4fd-5d33-b6e1-7b9efe3946fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9" :answer/id #uuid "e6c8494f-b16a-5986-b04a-52437f83ffe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064158 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7df42d1b-4cec-5d78-8cd7-de98b310c091"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7df42d1b-4cec-5d78-8cd7-de98b310c091" :question/id #uuid "7df42d1b-4cec-5d78-8cd7-de98b310c091" :question/math-academy-id "q-166771" :question/problem "A meter of drill fabric costs $$3.48.$ If Anna bought one meter of cotton fabric and one meter of drill fabric, in total, she paid $$${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In part 2, we found that one meter of cotton fabric costs $$3.95.$\n\nTo find the total cost, we need to calculate the value of $3.95+3.48.$\n\nFirst, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n3.95+3.48=7.43.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total cost is $$7.43.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-473457c1-8e08-59c3-a98c-5f53900769e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-473457c1-8e08-59c3-a98c-5f53900769e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "473457c1-8e08-59c3-a98c-5f53900769e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1" :answer/id #uuid "f42abcde-18da-58ae-82a1-21e9df0d6cc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138340 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43e5a6a2-9436-51e4-a444-4829716961e6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-43e5a6a2-9436-51e4-a444-4829716961e6" :question/id #uuid "43e5a6a2-9436-51e4-a444-4829716961e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-166772" :question/problem "Carmen, an experienced seamstress, bought $15\\,\\text{m}$ of drill fabric. The total she paid, expressed as a **decimal number**, was $$${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find out the amount of money that Carmen must pay, we need to multiply $15$ by $3.48.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere are $2$ decimal places in $3.48.$ \nTherefore, the product will also have $2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $5220$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n52\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{20}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Carmen must pay $$3.48\\times 15=$52.20.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-702a575b-0f02-5112-9f67-849c6e333818"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-702a575b-0f02-5112-9f67-849c6e333818" :answer-field/id #uuid "702a575b-0f02-5112-9f67-849c6e333818" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516" :answer/id #uuid "5bb55442-b865-5577-b007-562ca745e516" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142811 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e72e7ec5-9f77-5705-95ed-eadc3761bae8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e72e7ec5-9f77-5705-95ed-eadc3761bae8" :question/id #uuid "e72e7ec5-9f77-5705-95ed-eadc3761bae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-166773" :question/problem "Carmen cuts a piece of drill fabric with a length of $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}$ to make a tablecloth. If the fabric has a width of $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m},$ what will be the area of the tablecloth? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe tablecloth will have an area of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The tablecloth will have an area of $(2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}){\\text{m}}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{4\\times 2}=\\frac{27}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{8}=3\\,\\text{R}3=3\\,\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-10ea190f-2b81-55d5-aae9-2f2c1fbbbaf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-10ea190f-2b81-55d5-aae9-2f2c1fbbbaf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "10ea190f-2b81-55d5-aae9-2f2c1fbbbaf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8" :answer/id #uuid "80e8c721-00c6-52fa-9c87-aa630d796ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138377 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d13eae43-32e2-575a-85c2-71abf6bbd783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d13eae43-32e2-575a-85c2-71abf6bbd783" :question/id #uuid "d13eae43-32e2-575a-85c2-71abf6bbd783" :question/math-academy-id "q-166774" :question/problem "Carmen cuts two pieces of drill fabric with lengths of $\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\text{m}$ and $\\frac{9}{7}\\,\\text{m}.$ The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is{{field-1}}$\\text{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $(\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7})\\text{m}.$\n\nTo add two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nLet's look at the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nThe least common denominator of $6$ and $7$ is $42.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{5}{6}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{5\\times 7}{6\\times 7}=\\frac{35}{42}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{9}{7}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 6}{7\\times 6}=\\frac{54}{42}\n$$\n\nWe can now add the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we add the numerators.\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{42}+\\frac{54}{42}=\\frac{89}{42}\n$$\n\nExpressing this fraction as a mixed number, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{89}{42}=2\\,\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $2\\,\\frac{5}{42}\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d8ed4fae-048d-5f03-b27c-895a7582dfc5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d8ed4fae-048d-5f03-b27c-895a7582dfc5" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ed4fae-048d-5f03-b27c-895a7582dfc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c" :answer/id #uuid "8a68bafd-e384-5f9b-83b4-e06cb2184c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{89}{42}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138577 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-86788b5f-c043-547d-a152-64c87d27af72"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-86788b5f-c043-547d-a152-64c87d27af72" :question/id #uuid "86788b5f-c043-547d-a152-64c87d27af72" :question/math-academy-id "q-166775" :question/problem "Carmen has a piece of fabric with a length of $5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}.$ She accidentally spills coffee on this piece, so she decides to cut out and discard $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{m}$ of fabric. How long is the remaining piece of fabric? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe remaining piece of fabric has a length of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}.$" :question/worked-solution "The new piece of fabric has a length of $(5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5})\\text{m}$ long.\n\nTo subtract two mixed numbers, we subtract whole numbers from whole numbers and fractions from fractions.\n\nSubtracting the whole numbers, we get $5-1=4.$ \n\nNow we subtract the fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nLet's look at the denominators. The least common denominator of $4$ and $5$ is $20.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{5}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{1\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{4}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{5}{20}-\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=4\\,\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16254907-0b98-5e04-a2ea-99f6a0c12803"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16254907-0b98-5e04-a2ea-99f6a0c12803" :answer-field/id #uuid "16254907-0b98-5e04-a2ea-99f6a0c12803" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829" :answer/id #uuid "5adf5daf-1367-5822-9ec3-09c2b43dc829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\frac{1}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "multistep-1d647fef-1d2c-50b3-84cd-f7252db446b1" :multistep/id #uuid "1d647fef-1d2c-50b3-84cd-f7252db446b1" :multistep/context "A store ordered $1\\,955\\,\\text{m}$ of fabric, for which it received $23$ identical rolls." :multistep/steps ["step-f03e0c40-904e-5370-ae2b-e7895a0cd2d7" "step-d15708ef-cb23-5891-a11f-5eaa2241a771" "step-589511b7-0670-5b54-986c-f2be952afaeb" "step-a35324a4-a1b7-5b6d-8c10-28e06c42be8f" "step-d75c4c3b-0310-5bdf-b879-77ce82b6faef" "step-50c3a137-4d94-52b4-89d4-6b6356bc224a" "step-318a93bb-aab6-5b65-8bfa-538cbcc6cd3c"] :multistep/first-step "step-f03e0c40-904e-5370